---
alwaysApply: false
name: vite-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for Vite applications and environment management
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}
---

- Use `import.meta.env.VITE_*` for environment variables; avoid `process.env`.
- Keep Vite version consistent across the project; only include in `devDependencies`.
- Normalize headers to lowercase on ingestion for consistency.

---
name: react-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for React applications and component management
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}
---

- Use functional components and hooks for state management.
- Implement error boundaries to catch errors in the component tree.
- Ensure all interactive elements have appropriate `aria-labels` for accessibility.

---
name: typescript-best-practices.mdc 
description: TypeScript coding standards and type safety guidelines
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx}
---

- Use strict null checks to avoid runtime errors.
- Prefer interfaces over types for defining object shapes.
- Implement type guards and assertions for better type safety.

---
name: accessibility-best-practices.mdc
description: Guidelines for accessibility in web applications
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,html}
---

- Ensure all interactive controls have focus rings and appropriate `aria-labels`.
- Use modals that trap focus and restore focus on close; allow ESC to close.
- Implement keyboard shortcuts for common actions, providing visual feedback.

---
name: testing-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for testing in JavaScript applications
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}
---

- Write unit tests for utility functions and critical components.
- Use snapshot testing for UI components in various states.
- Maintain a manual QA checklist for edge cases and performance testing.

---
name: security-best-practices.mdc
description: Security guidelines for web applications
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}
---

- Avoid logging sensitive information; guard debug logs with a development flag.
- Run scripts in a Web Worker sandbox to isolate untrusted code.
- Clearly label any simulated data to avoid confusion.

---
name: performance-best-practices.mdc
description: Performance optimization strategies for web applications
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}
---

- Measure performance before optimizing; avoid premature optimizations.
- Use lazy loading for components and routes to improve initial load times.
- Optimize rendering by using React.memo and useCallback where appropriate.